{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:30:48Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 13, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t# Spec: Search tasks by title\n2\t\n3\t**Taiga:** #11\n4\t**Type:** Feature\n5\t**Branch:** feature/tp-11/search-tasks-by-title\n6\t\n7\t## Goal\n8\t\n9\tLet me type into a search box to narrow the visible task list down to tasks\n10\twhose title matches what I typed, so a long list stays usable.\n11\t\n12\t## Acceptance criteria\n13\t\n14\t1. **Given** tasks exist, **when** I type text into the search input,\n15\t   **then** only tasks whose title contains that text remain visible in the\n16\t   list.\n17\t2. **Given** I type text in a different case than the title (e.g. \"MEET\"\n18\t   against a task titled \"Team meeting\"), **when** filtering runs, **then**\n19\t   it still matches \u2014 matching is case-insensitive.\n20\t3. **Given** the search matches a substring anywhere in the title (not just\n21\t   the start), **when** filtering runs, **then** the task is shown \u2014 e.g.\n22\t   \"meet\" matches \"Team meeting\".\n23\t4. **Given** a state filter (Open/Done/All) is active and I also type a\n24\t   search term, **when** both are active, **then** the list shows only\n25\t   tasks that satisfy *both* \u2014 the same task-list array is narrowed by\n26\t   state first, then by title, exactly as `visibleTasks` already narrows by\n27\t   state in `frontend/src/App.jsx:29`. Search and state filter combine with\n28\t   AND, never override or reset each other.\n29\t5. **Given** my search term matches zero tasks under the current state\n30\t   filter, **when** the list would otherwise render, **then** an explicit\n31\t   message says nothing matched the search \u2014 distinct from the existing\n32\t   \"Nothing to do yet.\" / \"Nothing open right now.\" / \"Nothing done yet.\"\n33\t   copy in `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx:3-7`, which means \"this\n34\t   state filter is empty,\" not \"your search found nothing.\"\n35\t6. **Given** I clear the search input back to empty, **when** filtering\n36\t   runs, **then** all tasks reappear (subject only to the state filter).\n37\t7. **Given** the task list re-fetches after an add/complete/delete/edit\n38\t   (`refresh()` in `App.jsx:16`), **when** the refresh completes, **then**\n39\t   my typed search term is not cleared \u2014 it behaves like `filter`, which\n40\t   already survives refreshes because both live in `App` state, not in\n41\t   fetched data.\n42\t\n43\t## Non-goals\n44\t\n45\t- No backend involvement. The state filter has no server-side support today\n46\t  \u2014 `store.list()` (`backend/app/store.py:51`) always returns everything,\n47\t  and `App.jsx` narrows it client-side. Search follows the same pattern:\n48\t  no new query param, no new endpoint, no changes under `backend/`.\n49\t- No fuzzy or typo-tolerant matching. Literal case-insensitive substring\n50\t  only, per the request's own wording (\"case-insensitive... what is\n51\t  actually displayed\").\n52\t- No matching against fields other than the displayed title \u2014 not `id`,\n53\t  not `priority`.\n54\t- No highlighting of the matched substring inside the title.\n55\t- No debouncing/throttling the input. The store is in-memory with no\n56\t  pagination, and filtering is a synchronous array pass over data already\n57\t  in memory \u2014 the same cost the state-filter buttons already pay on every\n58\t  click.\n59\t- No persistence of the search term across a page reload. It is transient\n60\t  UI state, same lifecycle as `filter` (`App.jsx:14`), which also doesn't\n61\t  persist today.\n62\t- Does not change sort order \u2014 the existing high-priority-first sort\n63\t  (`App.jsx:35-37`) still applies to whatever the combined filters leave.\n64\t\n65\t## Affected areas\n66\t\n67\t- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 add a `search` state value alongside `filter`\n68\t  (line 14); extend the `visibleTasks` filter (lines 29-33) to also test\n69\t  the title; pass `search`/`setSearch` to the new search input and down to\n70\t  `TaskList`.\n71\t- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 `EMPTY_COPY` (lines 3-7) is\n72\t  keyed only by `filter`; needs a search-aware empty-state message per AC5.\n73\t- A new component under `frontend/src/components/` for the search input\n74\t  itself (placement/naming is a UX decision \u2014 it's a text input, not a\n75\t  toggle-button group, so it doesn't belong inside the existing\n76\t  `TaskFilter.jsx`, which renders `role=\"group\"` buttons).\n77\t- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 styling for the new input, likely extending\n78\t  `.list-toolbar` (`App.css:33`) where `TaskFilter` and `ClearCompleted`\n79\t  already sit.\n80\t- No changes to `backend/` (see Non-goals).\n81\t\n82\t## Edge cases\n83\t\n84\t- **Empty store (no tasks at all):** falls through to the existing\n85\t  per-filter empty copy, not the new \"no search matches\" copy \u2014 there's\n86\t  nothing to have searched yet. Distinguish \"0 tasks total\" from \"0 tasks\n87\t  after search narrowed a non-empty list.\"\n88\t- **Search text with no tasks matching, under `filter=all` vs `open` vs\n89\t  `done`:** the \"no matches\" message applies in all three combinations\n90\t  (AC4 + AC5 together).\n91\t- **Whitespace-only search term:** should not throw or behave oddly;\n92\t  treating it as matching everything (empty-after-trim behaves like no\n93\t  search) is a reasonable default consistent with typical search-box UX.\n94\t- **Special characters in the search term** (e.g. `(`, `*`, `.`): must be\n95\t  treated as literal text to match, not a regex \u2014 a title containing\n96\t  literal `(` should be findable by typing `(`, and typing regex\n97\t  metacharacters must never throw.\n98\t- **Search term longer than any title, or containing characters no title\n99\t  has:** zero matches, same \"no matches\" message as AC5.\n100\t- **Clearing search while a state filter is still active:** returns to\n101\t  exactly the state-filtered list (AC6), not the unfiltered full list.\n102\t\n103\t## Open questions\n104\t\n105\tNone \u2014 the request is unambiguous enough to proceed on the defaults stated\n106\tabove (substring match, AND-combine with the state filter, transient\n107\tclient-side state). Exact placement and copy for the search input and the\n108\tnew empty-state message are UX decisions for the next stage, not product\n109\tdecisions requiring sign-off.\n110\t", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_015g6Rm4cZppXqGo6sRc8m5u", "session_id": "c61f2e14-8069-45c7-82e4-a0377a07e709"}}
