ltering algorithm, and CSS verbatim.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `npm run build` (Vite production build) passed cleanly \u2014 23 modules transformed, no errors. This exercises JSX parsing/compilation across all touched and new files.\n- `npm run lint` (oxlint) \u2014 **could not run**: every invocation I tried (`npm run lint`, `npx oxlint src`, the `./node_modules/.bin/oxlint` binary directly) came back `This command requires approval`, in a headless session with no one able to grant it. This is a tooling/session limitation, not a code issue \u2014 I did not skip it by choice. Please run `cd frontend && npm run lint` before merging to confirm.\n- No frontend test framework exists in this repo (`package.json` has no `test` script, no test deps, and no existing component has a test file), so there was nothing to add a test to or run \u2014 consistent with the rest of the codebase.\n- Not manually exercised in a browser in this session (no browser tool available here); the design doc's wireframes cover every state (populated/narrowed/combined-with-filter/no-match/cleared/empty-store/loading/focus). Recommend a quick manual pass: `cd frontend && npm run dev`, type into the search box while toggling Open/Done/All, and confirm the \u201cNo tasks match\u2026\u201d message and native \u00d7 clear button (Chromium/Safari) both behave as designed.\n\n**How to verify:**\n```\ncd frontend && npm run build   # passed\ncd frontend && npm run lint    # blocked in this session, please run manually\ncd frontend && npm run dev     # manual UI check\n```", "meta": {"native_type": "assistant", "block_type": "text", "session_id": "c61f2e14-8069-45c7-82e4-a0377a07e709"}}
